# Achievement System for Cursor

When notable coding milestones are reached, celebrate with an Xbox-style achievement notification.

## How to Trigger

Use Playwright browser tools to navigate to the achievement page with URL params:

```
browser_navigate to http://localhost:5052/achievement.html?title=TITLE&score=SCORE&desc=DESCRIPTION
```

Or use the shell script:
```bash
./unlock.sh "Title" score "Description"
```

## Achievement Triggers

Trigger achievements for these milestones:

| Event | Achievement | Score | Description |
|-------|-------------|-------|-------------|
| Deployed to production | Ship It! | 50 | Deployed to production |
| Fixed a bug | Bug Squasher | 25 | Fixed a nasty bug |
| All tests passing | All Green | 25 | All tests passing |
| First commit of session | Hello World | 15 | Made your first commit |
| PR merged | Merge Master | 25 | PR merged to main |
| Wrote documentation | Future You Thanks You | 20 | Wrote documentation |
| Coding after midnight | Night Owl | 10 | Coding past midnight |
| Coding before 7am | Early Bird | 10 | Coding before 7am |
| First sale/user | First Sale! | 100 | Someone paid real money |
| Refactored code | Clean Code | 30 | Refactored legacy code |

## URL Encoding

Remember to URL-encode spaces and special characters:
- Space → %20
- ! → %21
- ' → %27

Example:
```
?title=Ship%20It!&score=50&desc=Deployed%20to%20production
```

## Server Setup

Before triggering, ensure a server is running:
```bash
cd /path/to/achievement-unlocked-cursor-trophies
python3 -m http.server 5052
```

Or use the unlock script which handles this automatically.
